      "hints": [
        "Use the binomial theorem $(1+y)^5 = 1 + 5y + 10y^2 + \\dots$ with $y = 2x$.",
        "Evaluate $1 + 5(2x) + 10(4x^2)$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Apply the binomial expansion formula to $(1 + 2x)^5$ up to the term in $x^2$:\n$$(1 + 2x)^5 = 1 + \\binom{5}{1}(2x) + \\binom{5}{2}(2x)^2 + \\dots$$\n$$= 1 + 5(2x) + 10(4x^2) + \\dots = 1 + 10x + 40x^2$$"
      ],
      "checking": {
