      "hints": [
        "Multiply $(1 + 10x + 40x^2)$ by $(1 - 6ax + 15a^2x^2)$.",
        "Collect all products giving $x^2$: $1(15a^2) + 10(-6a) + 40(1) = 15a^2 - 60a + 40$.",
        "Set the coefficient equal to $-5$: $15a^2 - 60a + 40 = -5$.",
        "Solve $15a^2 - 60a + 45 = 0 \\implies a^2 - 4a + 3 = 0$ for $a$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Multiply the two expansions from part (a):\n$$(1 + 10x + 40x^2 + \\dots)(1 - 6ax + 15a^2x^2 + \\dots)$$",
        "Identify the three products that form the coefficient of $x^2$:\n$$1 \\cdot (15a^2) + 10 \\cdot (-6a) + 40 \\cdot (1) = 15a^2 - 60a + 40$$",
        "Set the coefficient equal to $-5$:\n$$15a^2 - 60a + 40 = -5 \\implies 15a^2 - 60a + 45 = 0$$",
        "Divide by $15$ and factorise the quadratic equation:\n$$a^2 - 4a + 3 = 0 \\implies (a - 1)(a - 3) = 0$$\n$$a = 1 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad a = 3$$"
      ],
